  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "What is the phase difference between two simple harmonic motions represented by $x_{1}=A \\sin \\left(\\omega t+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$ and $x_{2}=A \\cos (\\omega t) ?$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YjKB9",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OCnru",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uiFTC",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eXH29",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nx_{1}=A \\sin \\left(\\omega t+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\\\\r\nx_{2}=A \\cos (\\omega t) \\\\\r\nx_{2}=A \\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\omega t+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nPhase difference\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta \\phi=\\phi_{2}-\\phi_{1}\r\n$$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\Delta \\phi=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\\\\r\n\\Delta \\phi=\\frac{3 \\pi-\\pi}{6}=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
